  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONS OF STRATEGIC PROPERTIES IN QUEBEC&quot;S GREEN MOUNTAINS &amp; CAPACITY BUILDING III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Atlantic Northern Forest contains a wealth of natural resources, but these resources also face numerous threats: over 90% of the area is in private hands. Located within an hour&apos;s drive of Montreal, the largest city in Quebec, the pressure on the region&apos;s natural habitats for residential development, recreational activities and infrastructures is considerable. This project will protect in perpetuity 1,000 acres through either fee-simple or easement acquisition. Located in Quebec&apos;s Northern Green Mountains natural trans-border corridor, the targeted properties are strategically located in core areas of unfragmented forest, and form a crucial link maintaining connectivity between properties already protected in the region. The project will also build capacity with grantee partners, who carry out related work in the area.</narrative>
  </description>
